course: dictionary
lesson: 4620
title: One word, many meanings: highlight
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word highlight can mean different things, and the sentence tells you which one. Read the words around it for clues. «Shading makes parts darker where light does not reach... and the brightest spot is the highlight.» Here the brightest spot is the highlight, so it means a bright part of a picture.
explain: «Social media often shows only people's best moments, a "highlight reel".» Best moments is the clue, so a highlight here is the best part of something. «You never write, draw or highlight in a library book» uses highlight as an action word: to mark words with a coloured pen.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «You never mark words with a coloured pen in a library book» still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
fact: A highlight is the best or most exciting part of something.
fact: To highlight means to mark words with a bright colour pen so they stand out, as in «highlight key words».
fact: To highlight can also mean to point out or draw attention to something important.
fact: Highlights are lighter streaks in hair or bright parts of a picture.
fact: Highlights are short clips of the best moments of a match or event, like «match highlights».
exercise: «Shading makes parts darker where light does not reach... the brightest spot is the highlight.» In this sentence, what is the highlight? | *A bright spot where the light hits | A round object | A type of pen | A dark shadow
exercise: «You never write, draw or highlight in a library book, because it belongs to everyone.» What does highlight mean here? | *To mark words with a bright colour pen | To read it out loud | To hide it from other people | To borrow it for a week
exercise: Mrs Patel says, «Please highlight the key words in your text.» What does she want you to do? | Copy the text onto a new page | *Mark the key words so they stand out | Throw the text away | Read the whole text out loud
test: «Social media often shows only people's best moments, a "highlight reel".» What does highlight reel suggest? | A list of every mistake | *The best moments of something | A kind of camera | A recording of a whole day
test: «Chloe watches highlights with her phone in her lap.» What are highlights in this sentence? | A bright lamp | A list of rules | Pens for the library | *Short clips of the best moments of a match
exam: In «the highlight of the trip was the zoo», what does highlight mean? | *The best part | A dark shadow | A streak of lighter hair | A marker pen
